+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| **SECTION 2**                                                         |
|                                                                       |
| **General Digital Skills**                                            |
|                                                                       |
| For Learning · For Work · For Society                                 |
+=======================================================================+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

Drawn from the DfE Essential Digital Skills Framework and the
FutureDotNow AI-updated EDS (October 2025). The five core EDS categories
--- Communicating, Handling Information & Content, Transacting, Problem
Solving, and Being Safe & Legal Online --- cut across all three
contexts.

**For Learning**

**01 Navigating Digital Platforms**

Using VLEs (Moodle, Canvas), Microsoft Teams, SharePoint, and college
portals to access timetables, resources, and learning materials
independently.

**02 Research & Information Literacy**

Searching effectively using specific terms and multiple sources.
Evaluating source credibility, publication dates, and author authority.
Identifying AI-generated misinformation.

**03 Digital Note-taking & Organisation**

Using OneNote, Google Docs, or equivalent for organised, retrievable
notes. Creating folder structures and naming conventions for coursework.
Managing version history.

**04 Collaborative Digital Working**

Co-editing shared documents in real time, contributing to group Teams
channels, completing peer review tasks digitally, and managing
asynchronous collaboration.

**05 AI-Assisted Learning**

Using AI tools (ChatGPT, Copilot, Grammarly) to support research,
drafting, and self-quizzing --- with full understanding of academic
integrity and institutional AI policies.

**For the World of Work**

**01 Professional Communication**

Email etiquette, Teams/Zoom protocol, appropriate tone for digital
workplace communication. Understanding when to use different channels
(email vs message vs call).

**02 Productivity & Office Applications**

Confident use of Word, Excel (formulae, sorting, charts), and
PowerPoint. Saving to and sharing from cloud storage. Managing
scheduling with Outlook calendar.

**03 Digital Transactions & Invoicing**

Online payments, basic invoicing apps (Xero, Sage), submitting VAT
returns digitally, managing work-related financial records. HMRC Making
Tax Digital awareness.

**04 Data Handling & Record-Keeping**

Accurate digital data entry, understanding data protection (GDPR),
maintaining compliant records. Interpreting basic workplace data and
acting on findings.

**05 AI Literacy for the Workplace**

Using AI assistants to draft, summarise, and research. Evaluating
outputs critically. Understanding ethical use, prompt engineering
basics, and AI limitations.

**For Societal Inclusion**

**01 Accessing Public & Government Services**

Gov.uk digital services, Universal Credit portal, NHS App appointment
booking, local council online forms, and HMRC self-assessment. Essential
for independent living.

**02 Online Safety & Privacy**

Password managers, two-factor authentication, recognising phishing and
social engineering attacks, GDPR basics, reviewing social media privacy
settings actively.

**03 Digital Financial Inclusion**

Online banking, comparing energy/insurance providers digitally, avoiding
scams, understanding digital payment systems and contactless
transactions.

**04 Critical Engagement with Media**

Identifying misinformation, understanding algorithmic bias and filter
bubbles, responsible social media use, understanding sponsored content
vs editorial content.

**05 Digital Wellbeing & Accessibility**

Screen time management, understanding technology\'s impact on mental
health, using and creating accessible digital content (WCAG 2.2),
assistive technology awareness.

**Sources**

DfE Essential Digital Skills Framework:
gov.uk/government/publications/essential-digital-skills-framework

FutureDotNow AI-Ready Workforce Report (Oct 2025):
futuredotnow.uk/new-report-charts-path-to-ai-ready-uk-workforce/

Ipsos/Lloyds EDS for Work 2024:
ipsos.com/en-uk/essential-digital-skills-work-2024

